{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Day With Vanessa"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Good Day"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.<br/><br/>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/><br/>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br/>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The man <span class=\"strong\">who/that</span> called wanted to speak to Tom.</span><br/>Which man? The man who called.<br/>The clause <span class=\"italic\">who called</span> immediately follows <span class=\"italic\">man</span> - the noun it describes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The book <span class=\"strong\">which/that</span> I lent you was my father's.</span><br/>Which book? The book I lent you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Native speakers of English often omit the pronoun in object clauses. <br/>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The book I lent you was my father's.<br/>The exhibition we saw was enlightening.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The exhibition which we saw was enlightening, right Sal?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The park that we went to was so grassy."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Hypothetical Situations and Wishes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the present or future.<br/>You use a similar structure to talk about wishes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/>If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/>Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past verb + would/could"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" simple past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I married Peter,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be happy.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I exercised more,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I could be in better shape.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I were you,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I would be jumping up and down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also reverse the clauses:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I would be out more if I were you.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice that there is no comma when the result clause comes first. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/>Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/>You use a similar structure to talk about wishes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + <span class=\"strong\">wish</span>+ Simple Past tense "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I wish I had my camera.<br/>I wish we could do that every day. <br/>I wish I could dance as well as the go-go dancers. </span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "enlightening"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "giving someone knowledge"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The exhibition which we saw was enlightening."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "zodiac"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a repeating cycle of 12 years, with each year being represented by an animal and its attributes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you do some reading about your zodiac sign?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feature"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must be curious to find out what the horse's attributes are. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dramatic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "impressive; spectacular"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Their outfits were so dramatic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "vibrant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "lively; colorful; bright"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The colors were very vibrant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "crisp"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cool; fresh; invigorating (when talking about the weather)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The air was so crisp."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grassy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "covered with grass"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The park was so grassy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go-go dancer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a dancer who entertains crowds at nightclubs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wish could dance as well as the go-go dancers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le16ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Take turns with a partner acting out the following feelings and situations: angry, hungry, sad, excited, frustrated, scared."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can talk but don't say the adjective. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Watch your partner act and try to guess how he or she feels."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use a statement to express how you think your partner is feeling."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Act out some other feelings that you think of."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about hypothetical situations. "}, {"type": "text", "co